From: Local Infra <infra@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] loonggpu: preserve validated scanout placement

A GBM scanout BO can initially prefer GTT even though every page flip pins it
in VRAM.  After the flip is unpinned, the next render CS migrates it back to
GTT and the following flip copies the full frame to VRAM again.  Preserve the
domain selected by a successful scanout pin so the next CS keeps the BO in its
validated placement.  Failure paths and the forced-GTT fallback for shares
from another GPU are unchanged.
---
 loonggpu/loonggpu_dc_plane.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/loonggpu/loonggpu_dc_plane.c b/loonggpu/loonggpu_dc_plane.c
--- a/loonggpu/loonggpu_dc_plane.c
+++ b/loonggpu/loonggpu_dc_plane.c
@@ -56,6 +56,15 @@ static int dc_plane_helper_prepare_fb(struct drm_plane *plane,
 		return r;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A successfully pinned scanout BO has demonstrated that this domain
+	 * is valid.  Preserve it as the preferred domain after the later unpin;
+	 * otherwise a GBM framebuffer that initially preferred GTT is migrated
+	 * back to GTT by every render CS and immediately copied to VRAM again by
+	 * the next page flip.  Other-GPU shares retain their forced GTT domain.
+	 */
+	rbo->preferred_domains = domain;
+
 	r = loonggpu_bo_kmap(rbo, &fb_vaddr);
 	if (unlikely(r != 0)) {
 		loonggpu_bo_unpin(rbo);
